#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d8dc0-98eb-53d0-9e48-3b1c2d7f6308" :question/math-academy-id "e-4508" :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/843dcd4359e4b61eb9715966fbbe6c26363ab5cfc57c55f94b6a41a73ec7feb1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/b9ba240f93ee3ec8c02e9718d62342dca0e0855e24c7b34ed97758a6eb7c46b8.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/id #uuid "422d31ad-8caa-5ce2-a0e0-c905fcc2640d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4509" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/240a1d2f7f93ec808127c9fa1791a77a43fcd7c0c84505540acc81c8b9fbc6e1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/7850cbafc78f2cf2ce14ae7111064bf2f5a029f4d1b97b6d5ebfc09e7126f44e.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed74e342-44d5-5a0d-bdeb-29a74691c7ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} {:answer/id #uuid "e02d476b-35b4-58af-8881-8011cee132f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347170} {:answer/id #uuid "2b946cbc-ba6a-5d77-9082-330ea43c303d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347171} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d043da-6f7b-55c1-b88b-ff8128a46618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347172} {:answer/id #uuid "69ce5340-db64-5350-a1db-996233164143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed74e342-44d5-5a0d-bdeb-29a74691c7ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} :answer-field/id #uuid "004c4b14-e8aa-5080-b660-07820c96dec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c4565b1-69f9-5bcf-baa2-75d567dcc9de" :question/math-academy-id "q-102705" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y=1 \\\\ 2x-3y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c010b75-821c-58b3-afc9-00c0bf092020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347176} {:answer/id #uuid "0d33f3be-3f54-5335-bdb3-0bcd69118688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347177} {:answer/id #uuid "c00ee482-bf1f-5b49-903b-a43438da12f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347178} {:answer/id #uuid "c94f5b72-8f1c-52ff-8721-0636b25674ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347179} {:answer/id #uuid "4540b966-2966-5174-b7ea-f1a753ca4f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4540b966-2966-5174-b7ea-f1a753ca4f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347180} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b8138c2-031b-5275-a3f9-a7b36a06e3ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b97b4d5-838b-5cc5-a6ea-8c327bb5d331" :question/math-academy-id "q-32141" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=7 \\\\ 8x+y=7\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
